A '''Hopper''' jumps around the room, doing contact damage to Isaac. They jump slowly around the room until Isaac gets close to them, at which point they start chasing Isaac. They can jump across rocks and gaps.

Hoppers transform into Flaming Hoppers after touching a {{E|Fire Place}}, fire spawned from {{i|Fire Mind}} or  {{Dlc|r}}{{i|Red Candle}}, or if they touch a {{i|Hot Bombs}} bomb.{{clear}}

== Variations ==
=== Flaming Hopper ===
{{infobox monster
 | name           = Flaming Hopper
 | id             = 54
 | base hp        = 20
 | environment    = {{floor|Basement}}{{floor|Burning Basement}}<br>{{floor|Caves}}{{floor|Catacombs}}<br>{{floor|Depths}}{{floor|Necropolis}}{{floor|Dank Depths}}
 | replace        = {{dlc|a|Hopper}}
 | replace chance = 60%
 | replace notes  = in {{s|Burning Basement|n}}
 | behavior       = Quickly hops around the room, doing contact damage. Covers a larger distance than the regular Hopper.
}}

'''Flaming Hoppers''' behave similarly to normal Hoppers in that they will randomly hop around the room, following Isaac only when within a certain range. Unlike normal Hoppers, Flaming Hoppers have a larger range of detection and can hop both further and faster.

Flaming Hoppers will still take damage from the [[Status Effects#Burn|burning]] status effect.{{clear}}

=== Leaper ===
{{infobox monster
 | name        = Leaper
 | id          = 34
 | base hp     = 25
 | environment = {{floor|Caves}}{{floor|Catacombs}}{{floor|Flooded Caves}}<br>{{floor|Depths}}{{floor|Necropolis}}{{floor|Dank Depths}}<br>{{room|challenge}}
 | behavior    = Hops around the room, doing contact damage. Occasionally jumps high into the air, dropping down onto Isaac's position while firing 4 blood shots in the cardinal directions.
}}

'''Leapers''' behave similarly to Hoppers, hopping around the room and chasing Isaac when he gets close but can also jump into the air and land on Isaac's position, firing four blood projectiles in the cardinal directions upon landing.
{{clear}}

